in the upcoming comics logic data  science program we will focus on data  science skills that are utilized in  biomedical research as well as industry  the goal of this upcoming webinar will  be to cover some of the background  information including what types of  projects and what types of challenges  we'll be talking about and some aspects  of exploratory data analysis summary  visualization of data data mining and  machine learning every step of the way  there are explanations about what the  methods do and provide a variety of  options for a category of methods  so essentially reprobation  logical maps of analysis help make sure  that there are logical steps and each  method is explained with inputs and  outputs resulting in highly reproducible  workloads after the data is prepared we  will be talking about how to utilize  statistical properties of data to make  sure we spot trends and understand how  to prepare the data for analysis for  example we will cover different  visualization normalization techniques  how do we leverage them visual  information that we have in these  methods and how do we understand the  application of these types of  visualization techniques to help us  understand the data that we're dealing  with  later on to talk about other types of  exploratory data analysis tools and  other types of data visualization so for  example we'll talk about distribution of  data and find associations and  correlations between replicants so we'll  talk about what part of it is technical  noise what part of it is actually James  pression then we'll talk about how to  use regression to spot more complex  trends so we'll talk about how to use  the regression to spot complex trends  that go beyond just a comparison of two  different conditions and move on to  clusters how to understand the different  linkage methods distances and how to  understand the relationships between  clusters as well as a variety of  different types of clustering methods  the omnilogi